## Settings UI

`SettingsWindow.cs` + `Settings*.cs` partials (Providers, Music, Monitor, Devices, Shelf, ClipboardSync, Themes, Sensors, Hotkeys, Updates, …). XAML: `SettingsResources.xaml`.

## Cross-cutting

- Themes: `PanelTheme.cs`, `Core/PanelThemes*.cs` (incl. Daylight / follow Windows), `Core/Themes/*.json`
- Localization: `Core/Loc.cs`
- Settings model / migrations: `Core/Settings.cs`, `SettingsMigrations.cs`, `DataLocations.cs`
- Window rules: `ScreenPolicy.cs`, `Native/WindowsHost.cs` (fullscreen, exclusive, occupied/overlap)
- Updates: `Updates/GitHubUpdates.cs`, `Core/AppUpdates.cs`, `InstallerUpdates.cs`
- Hotkeys / tray: `App.Hotkeys.cs`, `Native/GlobalHotkeys.cs`, `TrayIcon.cs`
- Entry: `Program.cs`, `App.xaml(.cs)`

## Fork (Matti)

- Prefer new code under `src/BrimDeck/Matti/` (see that folder’s README): click-through hold, Cursor Agent indicator, usage trend graph.
- Fork MSBuild overrides: root `Directory.Build.props`; defaults in `ForkRepositoryMetadata.targets`.
- Branches: `main` = upstream mirror (currently v1.3.2); work lands on `matti` (`feat/*` / `fix/*` → `matti`).

## Search tips

- Feature name → start in `Core/` for logic, matching `MainWindow.*` / `Settings*` / `Native/` for UI and OS.
- Device brand protocol → `Core/Brands/<Brand>.cs`.
- Quota provider → `Core/<Name>Usage.cs` or script provider via Settings › Quotas.
